{"created": "2024-04-12T03:13:22.523871+00:00", "modified": "2024-08-29T09:47:25.153142+00:00", "id": 10963339, "conceptrecid": "10963338", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.10963339", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.10963338", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10963339", "metadata": {"title": "Project - Physics-informed neural network for lithium-ion battery degradation stable modeling and prognosis", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.10963339", "publication_date": "2024-04-12", "description": "<p>Here are the datasets for our publication entitled \"<a href=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-024-48779-z\">Physics-informed neural network for lithium-ion battery degradation stable modeling and prognosis</a>\" published in Nature Communications.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The object of this experiment is the 18650 nickel-cobalt-manganese (NCM) lithium-ion battery manufactured by \"LISHEN\". The chemical composition is LiNi<sub>0.5</sub>Co<sub>0.2</sub>Mn<sub>0.3</sub>O<sub>2</sub>. The nominal capacity of the battery is 2000 mAh, and the nominal voltage is 3.6 V. The charging cut-off voltage and discharging cut-off voltage are 4.2 V and 2.5 V, respectively. The whole experiment was conducted at room temperature.&nbsp; A total of 55 batteries were included in this experiment, conducted under 6 different charging and discharging strategies. The charging and discharging platform is ACTS-5V10A-GGS-D, and the sampling frequency for all data is 1Hz.</p>\n<p>Other details can be found in \"Data Introduction.pdf\" file.</p>\n<p>The <strong>Python Code</strong> for reading and preprocessing this dataset is available at: <a href=\"https://github.com/wang-fujin/Battery-dataset-preprocessing-code-library\">https://github.com/wang-fujin/Battery-dataset-preprocessing-code-library</a></p>\n<p>Summary of articles using the this dataset: <a href=\"https://github.com/wang-fujin/XJTU-Battery-Dataset-Papers-Summary\">https://github.com/wang-fujin/XJTU-Battery-Dataset-Papers-Summary</a></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>If you find this data helpful, please consider citing our paper:</p>\n<p>Wang, F., Zhai, Z., Zhao, Z.&nbsp;<em>et al.</em>&nbsp;Physics-informed neural network for lithium-ion battery degradation stable modeling and prognosis.&nbsp;<em>Nat Commun</em>&nbsp;<strong>15</strong>, 4332 (2024). https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-48779-z</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Wang, Fujin", "affiliation": "Xi'an Jiaotong University", "orcid": "0000-0003-0236-3705"}], "version": "V1", "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "10963338"}}]}}, "title": "Project - Physics-informed neural network for lithium-ion battery degradation stable modeling and prognosis", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10963339", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/10963339", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/10963339?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10963339", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10963339", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.10963339", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10963339/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10963338", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/10963338", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10963338", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.10963338", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:10963339/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:10963339/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10963339/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10963339/media-files", "archive": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10963339/files-archive", "archive_media": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10963339/media-files-archive", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10963339/versions/latest", "latest_htm